<!--
    Notification small icon: the orbit path and its body, as a silhouette.

    The status bar draws small icons as a single flat shape - only the alpha
    channel survives - so this carries no colour and no detail that would turn
    into a smudge at ~18px.

    Redrawn from the launcher mark rather than kept as the old ring-with-a-bar,
    which read as "prohibited" at a glance. ORBIS slows short-form video; it does
    not block anything, and an ongoing notification that looks like a ban sign
    says the opposite.

    Deliberately drops the centre orb that the launcher icon has. Rendered at
    18px in one colour, an orb wide enough to occlude the ring fills the hole and
    the whole mark collapses into an indistinct lozenge; the open ring is the
    only part that survives the downscale. Shrinking the orb instead re-creates
    the eye reading the launcher mark was shaped to avoid - a small dot centred
    in an open ring is a pupil. So the glyph keeps the tilt, the ring and the
    node, and lets the orb go.

    Proportions are also heavier than a straight scale of the 108dp mark: a
    5:27 stroke vanishes at status-bar size.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24"
    android:tint="#FFFFFFFF">

    <group
        android:pivotX="12"
        android:pivotY="12"
        android:rotation="-28">

        <path
            android:pathData="M2.5,12 a9.5,4.6 0 1,0 19,0 a9.5,4.6 0 1,0 -19,0"
            android:strokeColor="#FFFFFFFF"
            android:strokeWidth="2.2"
            android:strokeLineCap="round" />

        <path
            android:pathData="M19.6,12 a1.9,1.9 0 1,0 3.8,0 a1.9,1.9 0 1,0 -3.8,0"
            android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF" />
    </group>
</vector>
